card.statement:
(a) The set of Kronecker canonical forms of all pairs in a sufficiently small neighborhood of

\begin{equation}
\mc L_m \oplus
\mc L_n,\qquad m\le n
\end{equation}

consists of the pairs

\begin{equation}
\mc L_{m+r} \oplus
\mc L_{n-r},\qquad m+r\le n-r,\  r\ge 0.
\end{equation}

(b) Each pair <<ref:u5ga>> with $r>0$ is equivalent to a pair of the form

\begin{equation*}
\left(
\mat{L_m&0\\0&L_n},
\mat{R_m&0
\\\D_r(\varepsilon )^T&R_n}
\right)
\end{equation*}

(which is obtained by an arbitrarily small perturbation of <<ref:(1a)>>), in which $\D_r(\varepsilon )$ is defined in <<ref:rdpd>> and $\varepsilon$ is an arbitrary nonzero complex number.
